Data Types:
    Primitive Data Types
       -We will know in advance how much memory that particular data type will consume
       -We don't need object to use them
       -INTEGER NUMBERS[byte, short, int, long],
        byte - 1 byte or 8 bits
               -128 to 127

        DECIMAL NUMBER[float, double],
        SINGLE CHARACTER[char],
        true/false [boolean]

    Non-Primitive Data Types
       -We will not know in advance how much memory that particular data type will consume
       -We will need object to use them
       -Class, Object, String.......


       HOW TO CHOOSE DATA TYPE TO STORE A VALUE:
        1. are we going to use some mathematical operation over that numbers - pick int data type
        2. if we are not going to apply some mathematical operation on the numbers
            see if this number lies in the range of single or multiple data types
              if single range - pick it
              if multiple select the one that takes least memory



